{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"3275","artifact_type":"architect","name":"plan/architect-provider-neutral-cache-bypass.md@sha256:039f49cd154534611020d28a8b8eb502e1735d214f55b5d6dc887371a571bfbc"},"owner_reference":"3275","content":"# Architecture Spec: Provider-Neutral Cache-Bypass Option for backlog_list / backlog_view\n\nBacklog item: #3275\n\n**CORRECTION (post-T3 implementation, orchestrator-applied):** ADR-3 as originally written claimed\nno test asserted the previously-unconditional live check for a cached numeric-selector item. That\npremise was checked only against `tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` and was factually wrong \u2014\n52 tests across `backlog_core/tests/` (test_view_live_sections.py, test_view_over_budget_gate.py,\ntest_concurrent_writes.py, and others using the shared `_view_test_helpers.py::_configure_memory_view`\nfixture) assert exactly the opposite: that a cached numeric-selector item IS live-enriched\nunconditionally. ADR-3 and \u00a74.4 below are revised to **additive-only**: Case A/B (cached item +\nnumeric/#N/URL selector) keep their exact pre-existing unconditional behavior \u2014 `refresh` does not\ngate them. Only Case H (cached item + title-substring selector \u2014 previously impossible) is gated\nbehind `refresh`. This satisfies the item's own AC5 (\"no other tool's parameters or behavior\nregress\") without any test-file changes to the 52 tests, and still satisfies AC2 (both selector\nshapes get bypass-cache capability \u2014 numeric always did, title now can via `refresh=True`). The\nsections below reflect the corrected design; struck-through claims are retained only as history.\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\nTwo changes to the backlog MCP+CLI surface, both reusing existing reconciliation code with zero\nnew reconciliation logic:\n\n1. **Rename** `backlog_list`'s GitHub-specific `from_github` parameter to the provider-neutral\n   `refresh` \u2014 on the MCP tool, on `operations.list_items()`'s own kwarg, and on the sole internal\n   caller (`sam_schema/backlog.py:95`). CLI `list --refresh` is unaffected (already neutral).\n2. **Add** a `refresh: bool = False` parameter to `backlog_view` (MCP) and CLI `view`, threaded\n   into `operations.view_item()`. Its ONLY effect is enabling a live-backend check for a\n   title-substring selector that already resolves to a cached item (Case H below) \u2014 a capability\n   that does not exist today. A cached item found via numeric/`#N`/URL selector is, and remains,\n   always live-checked unconditionally, exactly as it already behaves today \u2014 `refresh` does not\n   change that path in any way.\n\n`backlog_list_followups`/CLI `list-followups` are **out of scope**, per the item's own Acceptance\nCriteria (see \u00a710 ADR-4).\n\n## 2. Architecture Overview\n\n```mermaid\nC4Context\n    title Cache-bypass capability \u2014 system context\n    Person(caller, \"MCP client / CLI user\", \"Agent or human verifying synced state\")\n    System(backlog, \"backlog_core\", \"MCP server + CLI, cache + reconciliation\")\n    System_Ext(github, \"GitHub Issues API\", \"Authoritative backend (one of several)\")\n    Rel(caller, backlog, \"backlog_view(refresh=true) / view --refresh\")\n    Rel(backlog, github, \"view_enrich_from_github() -> work_item_version()\", \"HTTPS\")\n```\n\nNo new modules, no new services, no new reconciliation entry points. The change is parameter\nplumbing plus one small conditional addition in `view_item()` (SS4.4).\n\n## 3. Technology Stack\n\nNo new dependencies. Uses existing FastMCP `Annotated[bool, Field(...)]` tool-parameter pattern\n(already used by `from_github`/`full_refresh`) and existing Typer `Annotated[bool, typer.Option(...)]`\nCLI pattern (already used by `--refresh`/`--full-refresh`).\n\n## 4. Component Design\n\n### 4.1 MCP `backlog_list` (server.py:1935) \u2014 unchanged from original spec\n\nRename the parameter in place \u2014 no new capability, pure rename. (See original T1 task for exact\ndiff; already implemented and committed.)\n\n### 4.2 `operations.list_items()` (operations.py:1766-1807) \u2014 unchanged from original spec\n\nAlready implemented and committed (T1).\n\n### 4.3 MCP `backlog_view` (server.py:2392) \u2014 new `refresh` parameter \u2014 unchanged from original spec\n\nAdd `refresh: Annotated[bool, Field(description=\"Bypass the local cache and validate against the\nlive backend for a title-substring selector that already resolves locally. Selectors that resolve\nvia a numeric/#N/URL match are always validated against the live backend regardless of this flag \u2014\nthat behavior is unchanged and predates this parameter. For GitHub, resolves content through the\nauthoritative head-pointer/audit-comment record, never the raw issue body.\")] = False`, forwarded\ninto `operations.view_item(..., refresh=refresh)`.\n\n**Description text corrected from the original spec draft** \u2014 it previously implied `refresh`\ngates the numeric-selector path too. It does not.\n\n### 4.4 `operations.view_item()` (operations.py:2854) \u2014 restructured branching (CORRECTED)\n\nAdd `refresh: bool = False` to the signature (after `section`).\n\n**Corrected behavior**: the existing unconditional live call for numeric/`#N`/URL selectors is\n**preserved exactly as it exists today** \u2014 `refresh` never gates it. The only new conditional\nbehavior is Case H: a cached item found via a title-substring selector (`issue_num` is falsy)\ngains an opt-in live check when `refresh=True`. This was previously impossible \u2014 no code path\nexisted for it \u2014 so no existing test can regress from adding it.\n\n```python\ndef _live_lookup_id(item: BacklogItem | None, issue_num: str | None, selector: str) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Resolve the identifier to pass to view_enrich_from_github() for a live check.\n\n    Precedence: an already-parsed numeric selector; else the cached item's own\n    known issue number/id (for a title-selector match \u2014 never the raw title\n    text, which the GitHub backend cannot resolve); else the raw selector\n    (bare beads nanoid with no local match yet). Returns None only when no\n    identifier of any kind is resolvable.\n    \"\"\"\n```\n\nContract (implementer fills this exact body):\n- `issue_num` truthy -> return it unchanged (existing numeric/#N/URL path).\n- else `item is not None`: return `str(item.number)` if `item.number` is set, else\n  `item.issue.lstrip(\"#\") or None` if `item.issue` is set, else `None`. (Implementation note from\n  T3: `BacklogItem` has no `.number` field in this codebase \u2014 only `.issue: str`. Use\n  `getattr(item, \"number\", None)` defensively; it always falls through to `item.issue` today. This\n  is a harmless spec/code discrepancy, not a defect \u2014 leave the defensive `getattr` in place.)\n- else (`item is None`): return `selector.strip() or None` (bare nanoid / string-id backends only).\n\nRestructured control flow (replaces operations.py:2912-2933):\n\n```python\nitem = find_item(get_config().backend.list_work_items(), selector)\nissue_num = parse_issue_selector(selector)\nresult: ViewItemResult = view_result_from_local_item(item) if item else ViewItemResult()\n\nif item:\n    if issue_num or refresh:\n        # issue_num truthy -> Case A/B, always live-check (unconditional, matches\n        #   pre-existing behavior exactly \u2014 refresh plays no role here).\n        # issue_num falsy (title selector) + refresh=True -> Case H, new opt-in\n        #   live-check that did not exist before this item.\n        live_id = _live_lookup_id(item, issue_num, selector)\n        enriched = view_enrich_from_github(result, live_id, repo) if live_id else False\n        if not enriched:\n            out.warnings.append(\n                \"backend unreachable \u2014 sections_index reflects provider-backed record, may be stale\"\n            )\n    result.groomed = item.metadata.groomed\nelif issue_num or get_config().backend.issue_id_type == \"string\":\n    live_id = _live_lookup_id(item, issue_num, selector)\n    enriched = view_enrich_from_github(result, live_id, repo) if live_id else False\n    if not enriched:\n        raise ItemNotFoundError(selector)\nelse:\n    raise ItemNotFoundError(selector)\n```\n\nTruth table (CORRECTED \u2014 A/B no longer gated; H is the only new conditional case):\n\n| Case | issue_num | item cached | refresh | Old behavior (pre-item) | New behavior |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| A | yes | yes | \u2014 | always live-checks | **unchanged** \u2014 always live-checks, `refresh` irrelevant |\n| B | yes | yes, enrich fails | \u2014 | warns, falls back to cache | **unchanged** |\n| C | yes | no | \u2014 | live discovery, no exception | unchanged |\n| D | yes | no, enrich fails | \u2014 | raises `ItemNotFoundError` | unchanged |\n| E/F | no (string-id backend) | no | \u2014 | live discovery via nanoid | unchanged |\n| G | no (non-string-id backend) | no | \u2014 | raises `ItemNotFoundError` | unchanged |\n| H | no (title selector) | yes | \u2014 | **no live check possible, ever** | live-checks only if `refresh=True` \u2014 the one new capability |\n\n52 existing tests in `backlog_core/tests/` (via `_view_test_helpers.py::_configure_memory_view`)\nassert Case A's unconditional behavior \u2014 this table's \"unchanged\" rows are the evidence those\ntests continue to pass with zero modification.\n\n### 4.5 CLI `view` (sam_schema/backlog.py:110-124) \u2014 unchanged from original spec\n\nNew `--refresh` flag, forwarded into `operations.view_item(..., refresh=refresh)`. Same semantics\nas \u00a74.3: only affects title-selector live-checking.\n\n## 5-3. (Sections 5 Data Architecture, 6 Type System Design, 7 Security Architecture unchanged from\noriginal spec \u2014 no data model changes, `refresh: bool` matches existing convention,\n`_live_lookup_id()` return type `str | None` is deliberate, no new attack surface.)\n\n## 8. Testing Architecture (CORRECTED scenario list for T4)\n\n**No changes needed to any of the 52 previously-existing `backlog_core/tests/` tests** \u2014 Case A/B\nis provably unchanged (see truth table above), so no rename-affected or regression list applies to\nthat directory.\n\n**Rename-affected (T2, already complete)**: unchanged from original spec \u2014 the `from_github`\u2192\n`refresh` keyword rename list in `tests/`, `tests_backlog/`.\n\n**New tests required (T4, revised)**:\n1. Cached item + title-substring selector + `refresh=True` -> `view_enrich_from_github` called,\n   identifier argument equals the item's `number`/`issue`-derived id, NOT the raw title string.\n2. Cached item + title-substring selector + `refresh=False` (new default) -> `view_enrich_from_github`\n   NOT called. This is the one true regression-risk case now \u2014 it locks in that Case H is opt-in.\n3. Cached item + numeric selector + `refresh=False` -> `view_enrich_from_github` IS called\n   (regression guard: confirms Case A stayed unconditional and was NOT accidentally gated).\n4. No cached item + numeric selector + `refresh=False` -> live lookup still fires, no\n   `ItemNotFoundError` (regression guard, Case C/D unchanged).\n5. No cached item + beads nanoid + `refresh=False` -> live lookup still fires (Case E/F unchanged).\n6. Cached item + title selector + `refresh=True` + item has neither `number` nor `issue` set ->\n   warning appended, no exception, `view_enrich_from_github` NOT called.\n\n(Original spec's scenario \"cached item + numeric selector + refresh=True -> called\" is now\nredundant with scenario 3 above, since numeric selectors are always live-checked regardless of\n`refresh` \u2014 merge them into one test if convenient.)\n\nServer/CLI forwarding tests (T5) are unchanged from the original spec \u2014 `refresh` still forwards\nend-to-end on both surfaces; only the underlying `view_item()` gating logic changed.\n\n## 9-11. (Sections 9 Distribution Architecture, 11 Scalability Strategy unchanged from original\nspec.)\n\n## 10. Architectural Decisions (ADRs) \u2014 ADR-3 REVISED, others unchanged\n\n**ADR-1, ADR-2, ADR-4, ADR-5: unchanged from original spec** (parameter name `refresh`; outright\nrename of `list_items`'s kwarg with no alias; `backlog_list_followups` deferred; no new\nreconciliation code).\n\n**ADR-3 (REVISED): `refresh` is additive-only \u2014 it never gates the existing unconditional\nnumeric-selector live call; it only enables the new title-selector live check.**\n\nOriginal ADR-3 claimed \"no test in `tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` asserts the\npreviously-unconditional numeric-selector live call for an already-cached item, so no test\nregression\" from gating Case A behind `refresh`. That check was incomplete \u2014 it did not search\n`backlog_core/tests/`, which contains 52 tests (via the shared `_view_test_helpers.py` fixture)\nthat DO assert Case A's unconditional behavior, discovered during T3's implementation and full-suite\nverification. One of them, `test_concurrent_writes.py::test_second_groom_write_does_not_clobber_first_sections_on_view`,\nis itself a regression guard whose explicit premise is that a numeric-selector view always prefers\nlive data \u2014 directly contradicting the original ADR-3.\n\nGating Case A would violate the item's own groomed Acceptance Criterion 5 (\"no other tool's\nparameters or behavior regress\"). The item's Acceptance Criteria never requested reducing default\nnetwork-call volume for numeric selectors \u2014 that was ADR-3's own invented goal, not a stated\nrequirement. The corrected design delivers everything the item's Acceptance Criteria actually ask\nfor (AC2: both selector shapes get bypass-cache capability) with a strictly smaller diff and zero\ntest-file changes to the 52 affected tests.\n\n## Documentation Updates (required, not optional \u2014 Acceptance Criteria item 6) \u2014 unchanged from\noriginal spec.\n"}